<article class="env-lemma" id="061S">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/061S">Lemma <span data-tag="061S">10.69.6</span>.</a> Let $(R, \mathfrak m)$ be a local Noetherian ring. Let $M$ be a nonzero finite $R$-module. Let $f_1, \ldots , f_ c \in \mathfrak m$ be an $M$-quasi-regular sequence. Then $f_1, \ldots , f_ c$ is an $M$-regular sequence. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      Set $J = (f_1, \ldots , f_ c)$. Let us show that $f_1$ is a nonzerodivisor on $M$. Suppose $x \in M$ is not zero. By Krull's intersection theorem there exists an integer $r$ such that $x \in J^ rM$ but $x \not\in J^{r + 1}M$, see Lemma <a href="/tag/00IP" data-tag="00IP">10.51.4</a>. Then $f_1 x \in J^{r + 1}M$ is an element whose class in $J^{r + 1}M/J^{r + 2}M$ is nonzero by the assumed structure of $\bigoplus J^ nM/J^{n + 1}M$. Whence $f_1x \not= 0$. 
    <p>
      Now we can finish the proof by induction on $c$ using Lemma <a href="/tag/061R" data-tag="061R">10.69.5</a>. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>